<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <PackageId>ProveSDK</PackageId>
    <Version>1.1.0</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v1.1.0:
- BREAKING: callProveVerify, provePrefillIdentity and callProveTrustScore take a ConsentStatus, sent as Consent-Status, instead of always sending optedIn
- BREAKING: Identity, Pre-Fill and TrustScore refuse a number with a leading or bracketed trunk 0, or a 00 prefix without a whole number after it, which was sent as a different number
- BREAKING: callProveTrustScore gives ValueNone, not ValueSome 0, for a number refused here
- FIXED: callProveVerify sent the state code as extendedAddress; it goes as region
- FIXED: request bodies are UTF-8, so names outside ASCII reach Prove intact
- FIXED: the sign-in form encodes its values
- FIXED: a sign-in that fails or gives no token sends nothing further and returns the failure
- FIXED: a non-200 answer without a readable error becomes an error naming the status
- FIXED: dates of birth and added timestamps are Gregorian whatever the culture
- FIXED: printing a license or an SMS or InstantLink request (%A, ToString) hides its keys and the person's number
- FIXED: Readme examples match the API
- FIXED: a UK number written +44 0 or 0044 0 drops the trunk 0; other country codes keep every digit
- FIXED: a 2xx answer with an unreadable or empty body on any data call is that call's failure, with the status and the body's length and kind, not an exception or a success
- FIXED: an answer of the typed InstantLink calls without a status is a failure, not a success with PhoneMatch = Yes
- FIXED: callProveVerify fails on a response without a readable verified, instead of isDone = true and an exception in the caller
- FIXED: failure text holds the status, the body's length and kind, and only named JSON error fields with digits and emails masked, never the body's text
- FIXED: a refused number isn't echoed whole: the failure gives its digit count and at most its last two digits
- BREAKING: Sms.send and InstantLink.generate refuse every number Identity refuses, such as 07700 900123</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>Tuomas Hietanen, Timothé Larivière</Authors>
    <Company>Welendus</Company>
    <PackageDescription>Unofficial Prove .NET Client</PackageDescription>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/thorium/ProveSDK</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageTags>Prove identity identity-verification verification kyc trustscore trust-score sms fintech api-client dotnet fsharp csharp</PackageTags>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <IsTestProject>false</IsTestProject>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <PackageReadmeFile>Readme.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="ProveSDK.Tests" />
    <None Include="Readme.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <Compile Include="Common.fs" />
    <Compile Include="Identity.fs" />
    <Compile Include="TrustScore.fs" />
    <Compile Include="SmsDelivery.fs" />
    <Compile Include="InstantLink.fs" />
  </ItemGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="FSharp.Data" Version="8.1.11" />
    <PackageReference Include="FSharp.Data.JsonProvider.Serializer" Version="1.0.7" />
    <PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.3" />
    <PackageReference Update="FSharp.Core" Version="10.1.201" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
